WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.520
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.830
In my sophomore year I
walked onto the crew team,

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:14.490
and it completely
changed my life.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.630
Having that outlet
for stress helps

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.180
me enjoy both parts of my
life, both the athletic

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.890
and the academic
side, a lot more.

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:28.340
[CHATTER, CLATTERING]

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.320
We really just have an
amazing team culture.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.445
I learn a lot from the
people that I'm around.

00:00:32.445 --> 00:00:34.070
They definitely
inspire me to be better

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.320
on the water and academically.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:43.810
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.720
Most of the undergrad residences
are within like a five

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.275
or so minute walk
from the boathouse.

00:00:48.275 --> 00:00:50.650
We're at the boathouse now,
and that's an undergrad dorm.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:01:07.990
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:10.810
We kind of all push each other
to become the fastest boats

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.180
that we can be, but
at the same time,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:15.880
in order to become the
best versions of ourselves,

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:18.550
we have to be supportive of
each other throughout the way.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:27.800
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.410
The entire crew just
rowing as one person,

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:33.890
you're all moving at
the exact same time.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:37.070
The oars are clicking in
exactly the same rhythm.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:40.310
The boat is surging through
the water at the tempo

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:40.895
that you set.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.860
That is just such an incredibly
magical moment that I've never

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.510
experienced anywhere else.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.280
We're Division One.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.660
In the spring
we'll definitely be

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.540
rowing against a bunch of
the Ivies and Dartmouth,

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.320
Georgetown.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:02.240
We have some races
out in San Diego.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:07.920
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.990
The Charles is definitely
a very historic river

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.310
in the rowing community.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.860
Head of the Charles is one of
the most well-known regattas

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.580
in the world.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.400
Going through all the bridges
and hearing about all the turns

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.590
that I've heard about for
so long and then just like

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:22.007
rowing that every single day,
it's like it never gets old.

00:02:22.007 --> 00:03:07.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:09.890
I'm sort of driven by the
competitive aspect of it.

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:12.460
I just love racing.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.250
In the fall we do
sort of the big,

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.650
name brand races like
the Head of the Charles.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.650
We go up to the Head of
the Fish in New York.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:24.910
Being completely gassed and
just dead after the finish line,

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.220
but then you see the other
boat two or three seats back,

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.040
that's a great feeling.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.900
You're erging for the
whole winter season

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:34.450
and then the payoff
is that moment when

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.280
you sprint in the
last 200 meters,

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:39.328
pass another boat by a hair,
and you get the medals,

00:03:39.328 --> 00:03:40.120
you get the trophy.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.270
[MUSIC PLAYING]

